</article-title><source>Oncologist</source><year>2007</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>610</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17522250</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b30-co15-6-279"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gridelli</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Maione</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Amoroso</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Clinical significance and treatment of skin rash from erlotinib in non-small cell lung cancer patients: results of an Experts Panel Meeting</article-title><source>Crit Rev Oncol Hematol</source><year>2008</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>155</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18083041</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="f1-co15-6-279" position="float"><label>FIGURE 1</label><caption><p>Kaplan&#x02013;Meier estimate of time to progression by grade of rash</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="co15-6-279f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-co15-6-279" position="float"><label>FIGURE 2</label><caption><p>Median second-line time to progression by patient subgroup. Adeno = adenocarcinoma; <sc>egfr</sc> = epidermal growth factor receptor; pos = positive mutational status; neg = negative mutational status.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="co15-6-279f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="tI-co15-6-279" position="float"><label>TABLE I</label><caption><p>Results of selected randomized phase <sc>iii</sc> trials in the second-line treatment of non-small-cell lung cancer</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Reference</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Agents</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Patients (<italic>n</italic>)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Arm</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Median cycles (<italic>n</italic>)</th><